# The 32-bit starts of the portable harness (plan 5.18.10 PX3, P-1a.i): an
# msil64 image is IL-only AnyCPU PE32 (plan 5.18.7), so a 32-bit host loads
# it, and the width guard at the top of <Module>::.cctor (T-P10) must stop
# it there. %msil_dotnet_x86 is msil-run.py with the x86 dotnet host (the
# caller adds --runtime-major 8 or 10, which writes the runtimeconfig);
# %msil_set_32bitreq copies an image with COR20 flag 0x2 (32BITREQUIRED)
# set, which makes the .NET Framework direct start of an AnyCPU .exe a
# 32-bit process. The images are assembled with %{portable_ilasm}
# (lit.local.cfg: %ilasm without -pe64 -x64), and Inputs/pe-flags.py reads
# their envelope. Checks:
# (1) The envelope: optional header magic 0x10b (PE32), machine 0x14c
# (I386), CorFlags 0x1 (ILONLY alone).
# (2) Inputs/pointer-size.il exits with sizeof(native int): 4 under the x86
# host on .NET 8 and .NET 10, 8 under the 64-bit host of %msil_exec.
# (3) Inputs/guard.il, the guard's shape: under the x86 host on .NET 8 and
# .NET 10 an unhandled exception whose stderr carries the first T-P10 text
# (.NET 8 wraps the throw from the module initializer in a
# TypeInitializationException; .NET 10 reports the
# PlatformNotSupportedException itself), and its entry point never runs; on
# the 64-bit host it exits 42. This is the failure path of (2)'s width
# check.
# (4) %msil_set_32bitreq: the copy has CorFlags 0x3 and IN is unchanged; the
# Framework direct start of the original is a 64-bit process (exit 8), of
# the copy a 32-bit one (exit 4), where the guard stops guard.exe. IN that
# is no PE image, a missing IN and a missing OUT are errors (exit 2) that
# write nothing; --runtime-major 0, --runtime-major with --netfx and with
# --runtimeconfig are usage errors.
# REQUIRES: msil-dotnet-x86, system-windows

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t

# (1)
# RUN: %{portable_ilasm} -dll -output=%t/ps.dll %S/Inputs/pointer-size.il
# RUN: %{portable_ilasm} -exe -output=%t/ps.exe %S/Inputs/pointer-size.il
# RUN: %{portable_ilasm} -dll -output=%t/guard.dll %S/Inputs/guard.il
# RUN: %{portable_ilasm} -exe -output=%t/guard.exe %S/Inputs/guard.il
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pe-flags.py %t/ps.dll > %t/flags.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pe-flags.py %t/ps.exe >> %t/flags.txt
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/pe-flags.py %t/guard.dll >> %t/flags.txt
# RUN: %{harness_check} equals %t/flags.txt "pe-flags: magic 0x10b machine 0x14c corflags 0x1" "pe-flags: magic 0x10b machine 0x14c corflags 0x1" "pe-flags: magic 0x10b machine 0x14c corflags 0x1"

